    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDoyMjA5NTI6SElHSExJR0hUOmFmYmIzMGQxOC0yZDRhLTQzZTQtYTE3OC1kMGI4YTBmYjRlMjA",
      "text": "more important than planting seeds or digging",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "1474",
      "page": "122",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDoyMjA5OTg6SElHSExJR0hUOmEzZWUxODM1Zi01NGVjLTQ1YzgtYWY5NC04NTJjNjVlYTVhY2Y",
      "text": "the latrine or establishing my routine of",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "1474",
      "page": "122",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDoyMjEwNDA6SElHSExJR0hUOmE3OGZkYmVjYS0yOWUxLTQ1MTItOGEzOS1lZWM4MzlhM2JiNmQ",
      "text": "daily living, I needed to quiet my mind.",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "1474",
      "page": "122",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDoyMjQ0OTk6SElHSExJR0hUOmFhZWM2ZmE4NC03ZTBmLTQ5YmEtYTFiMi0wZWJmYjU2N2NjZmM",
      "text": "indescribable immensity",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "1497",
      "page": "124",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDoyMjQ1MjY6SElHSExJR0hUOmE4NzA3NmI3NS02MmYwLTRmM2ItODQ4Zi03NGE3Mjk1MDkxZDU",
      "text": "which I felt a part.",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "1497",
      "page": "124",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDoyNzAxNDc6SElHSExJR0hUOmFhYjUyMGE5My0zZTBmLTRkOTktYTFkYy00NTIzMTc5YjkzMTA",
      "text": "Falling in love with Wilson Moon had",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "1801",
      "page": "151",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDozMzQ1ODM6SElHSExJR0hUOmE3NTJkZDcwZC0zZjlhLTRiYmQtODJhOS00NDNlZGViNjlhNzU",
      "text": "I, the obedient girl; Seth, the angry",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "2231",
      "page": "185",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDozNDkyNTI6SElHSExJR0hUOmEwYTk4Y2Y0Yi05ODQ4LTQwMmItYTE0Mi1hYmVlOGVkZGU3N2Y",
      "text": "I never stopped questioning the choices of my past, but in the known world, each step surely unfurls the next, and we must walk into that open space, mapless and without invitation.",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "2329",
      "page": "192",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDozNTM1OTQ6SElHSExJR0hUOmExYzUyOGZkNS0yYTg2LTRkZjQtODRjZS1iN2U1MDg1NjMxYTA",
      "text": "truck and got out to take one long, final look at the place",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "2358",
      "page": "196",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDozNTM2NTQ6SElHSExJR0hUOmFjNGJlOTNlZi04NzkwLTQ0ZDQtYjA4Yi0xMjFmYmI4Yjc1ZTI",
      "text": "that made me.",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "2358",
      "page": "196",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDozNjY5MTQ6SElHSExJR0hUOmE3MGE1OWVmNS0wY2QzLTRhODMtOTdjMC05ZjhlNzZjZWYzNDc",
      "text": "teach him that one place is not the",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "2447",
      "page": "203",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDozNjY5NTA6SElHSExJR0hUOmFlN2NhMjBkNy0zYTkxLTRmNzQtODczNy1mOWJhNmJlZjU0YzU",
      "text": "same as any other, that this small patch of the vast and unknowable world was where we were held as kindred.",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "2447",
      "page": "203",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDozNzg5ODY6SElHSExJR0hUOmFjZjZmZmMxMC1hMTk3LTQxMzUtODZjOC02NGU3YzJkOWMxNjI",
      "text": "Wil had often encouraged me to lie back on the earth rather than sit, to feel my whole body against the ground and gaze up at the sky, and I did so that day just for the pleasure of absorbing the world.",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "2527",
      "page": "209",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDozODQ4MTc6SElHSExJR0hUOmE1YjVhNTNmNS05YjYxLTRiODUtOTkzZC0yNTk1ZjgyODRjNjg",
      "text": "My days had not felt so expansive since that early summer in the mountain hut when I first learned to trust the hours instead of fill them.",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "2566",
      "page": "213",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDozODU5MjM6SElHSExJR0hUOmE4MDkxZGM3MC03NjRkLTQ5ZWMtYWQwNS0wNDdhNmU2MGI0YTE",
      "text": "Each day, I was building a life of my choosing, and it was a good life. I knew what was missing, but I was also appreciative of what was there.",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "2573",
      "page": "214",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDozODkwNzE6SElHSExJR0hUOmEwOTllODAyNy0wMDU1LTQ5YjktYmRhMC1lMzI3YjIwMzUwMmU",
      "text": "Troubles came and went, like troubles do.",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "2594",
      "page": "215",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDo0MjI3Mzk6SElHSExJR0hUOmExMDgyMDg3NS0wNTZjLTRjNjEtOWEyOC05OTBkMzA2MmNhM2Q",
      "text": "frankness of a woman completely at ease with her own troubled past, I was heartbroken for my friend, but I was mostly jealous of her unfiltered honesty, her utter lack of self-blame.",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "2819",
      "page": "232",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDo0MjcyMjE6SElHSExJR0hUOmE3Nzk2NGE5My01Zjk4LTRhOTYtODM2ZS0zOTU5OWRjYzdlODg",
      "text": "But carrying your sorrows all alone isn’t strength, V. It’s punishment, plain and simple. Whatever happened to you, you’ve got to stop blaming yourself.”",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "2849",
      "page": "235",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDo0MzI1NTg6SElHSExJR0hUOmE0MjYyYmFlYS0wYzA1LTRmNDMtOGUwZS1lNWYyMWI1OTNlYTk",
      "text": "an opening that changed everything.",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "2884",
      "page": "237",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDo0NDQyMzA6SElHSExJR0hUOmE2MDgzZmVmYi1lZWMwLTRiMDUtYTJkMS0yZTcwYjU5ZTlkZWU",
      "text": "When he proposed, I felt dizzy and mistook that for love.",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "2962",
      "page": "247",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDo0OTIwMzk6SElHSExJR0hUOmFhNGU0OWJmMi04YzA3LTRmMzUtYmU5OS05ZDUyNmUwNDFiYzA",
      "text": "You stare at your arms and marvel that you are still flesh when by all right and desire the officers’ words should have turned you to ash.",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "3281",
      "page": "269",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDo0OTg3ODc6SElHSExJR0hUOmEwMzkwYTY4OS1jMTQzLTRiOGEtODY2YS1iNzdkOTU0ZjEzMTk",
      "text": "Sometimes a woman splits in two.",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "3326",
      "page": "272",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDo1MDY4MjQ6SElHSExJR0hUOmE0NWEwNDkyYy1iZGRjLTRhNGQtOTE5OS1jNDFmZTNmZWQ0ZDQ",
      "text": "I wished my story could flow so easily.",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "3379",
      "page": "280",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDo1MDk2NjQ6SElHSExJR0hUOmEwZDQ0NDkyMy1mMGQwLTRkMmMtYTZmOS0xODc5YmY0N2MyMmE",
      "text": "disbelief that the girl in the story—this Torie—was actually me, and that the whole tale had resided within me like a locked diary these many years.",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "3398",
      "page": "282",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDo1MjAzNTk6SElHSExJR0hUOmE0ZGYwYjgzMi05YWM2LTQwODEtOTk4OS0xYThmZTNjODFhMWQ",
      "text": "Women endure. That’s what we do.”",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "3470",
      "page": "287",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDo1MjA1MTk6SElHSExJR0hUOmE5ODFkMWU5OC03NWNjLTRlMWMtOGZiNS03OTM4ZDc3ZDVjNGQ",
      "text": "“A woman is more than a vessel meant to carry babies and grief.”",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "3471",
      "page": "287",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDo1MjUyMDU6SElHSExJR0hUOmE4ZjIwMWRhYi02MzBkLTQ1ZDMtOGE2NS00YmY1ZjBjZjAyNWY",
      "text": "Strength, I had learned, was like this littered forest floor, built of small triumphs and infinite blunders, sunny hours followed by sudden storms that tore it all down. We are one and all alike if for no other reason than the excruciating and beautiful way we grow piece by unpredictable piece, falling, pushing from the debris, rising again, and hoping for the best.",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "3502",
      "page": "289",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDo1MzQ0NDQ6SElHSExJR0hUOmE4NmQwZmFiNC00ZTQ4LTQyZGUtYjdmOC1kZTY0Y2VkM2Y2NWM",
      "text": "they were like many families, their lives together a weave of sad and complex and happy and sweet and tragic all at once.",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "3563",
      "page": "296",
      "source": "kindle"
    },
    {
      "id": "QTFSNVNUQkdPWkxYVUk6QjBCNzFDMTdSNDo1NDMyOTU6SElHSExJR0hUOmE0ZGI0MWM5Yy0zZGZhLTQyMjQtODQ1MS0xY2U2OGY4ZTQwNzA",
      "text": "my rising wisdom understood that I must carry my whole past alongside the new space I had created in myself for hope.",
      "color": "yellow",
      "location": "3622",
      "page": "300",
      "source": "kindle"
    }
  ]
}
